## User preferences

- When research was requested, the task required "short, evidence-based" answers with source links/dates and "no filler" -> cite primary sources, distinguish evidence from inference, and provide separate research documents plus the final report. [Task 2]
- The user first required stopping after each milestone, then instructed completion of M2-M4 in one turn -> follow the latest milestone/turn instruction while continuing to write `.coord/STATUS.md` checkpoints. [Task 2]
- For the queued-message test, the user said "reply briefly and append this exact message" -> preserve exact text in the designated coordination file and keep the chat acknowledgement concise. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- T-001 recommended GO for a disposable Avalonia + AvaloniaEdit spike and conditional GO for a disposable GPUI + GPUI Kit spike; neither is the final selected stack. The mandatory first gate for either is real Windows Precision Touchpad behavior: 1:1 movement, finger-release distance/velocity, inertia, cancellation, rubber-band overscroll, note creation, and coexistence with vertical editor scrolling/text selection. [Task 2]
- AvaloniaEdit extension seams include `TextView.ElementGenerators`, `VisualLineElementGenerator`, and `InlineObjectElement`; it has TextMate, folding, and line-number support. Avalonia Windows docs cover `Transparent`, `AcrylicBlur`, `Mica`, `WindowDecorations=None`, tray integration, and Win32 hooks, but public wheel APIs do not establish PTP begin/end/cancel lifecycle. [Task 2]

