## Delivered

- Three structurally different, real Avalonia directions: **Quiet** (unified writing surface), **Card** (elevated note/peeks/floating pager), **Pro** (compact toolbar/numbered gutter/status/command hints).
- "'`src/AntiQuickPad/Design/DesignEntry.cs`, `DesignSpec.cs`, `DesignWindow.cs`, `ChevronMargin.cs`. Only two small normal-source hooks: Program dispatches the design/probe flags; App creates the isolated design or probe window. Normal resident creation is unchanged.
- `--render-design <quiet|card|pro> <outdir>` uses real production EditorFactory, Markdown/Python transformer, code background, checkbox/guide/strike renderers and folding manager; adds a regular base-typeface transformer, active-line renderer and clickable custom chevron margin in the design host.
- 30 PNGs: three directions × main/bars/menu/carousel/empty × 1×/1.5×. **Viewed every final PNG individually** after repairs. Correct 960×800 / 1440×1200 dimensions and SHA256 recorded in `docs/design/m6/render-manifest.json`.
- `docs/design/m6/README.md`: every PNG linked, three-line pitches, layout/type/icon/gutter/code/checkbox/scrollbar details, differences vs today, per-direction motion proposals/difficulties, known limits, effort estimates, reproduction/probe instructions and final comparison table.
- `--probe-backdrop <none|mica|acrylic|blur>` opens an independent real standard-chrome window with semitransparent background. Optional `--report path` and `--close-after-ms n` allow graceful capability recording; without the latter it stays open for human inspection.

## Evidence

Final Release build: **0 warnings, 0 errors** (`docs/design/m6/build.log`). Used the requested quit-before-build routine and offline build flags. A build attempted while the isolated selftest still owned the apphost encountered a sharing lock; allowed the selftest to finish, then rebuilt cleanly. No process was killed.

Final selftest: PENDING_FINAL_RESULT

Backdrop capability reports, OS API string `Microsoft Windows 10.0.26340`, Avalonia `12.1.4.0`:

| Requested mode | ActualTransparencyLevel |
|---|---|
| none | None |
| mica | Mica |
| acrylic | AcrylicBlur |
| blur | Transparent |

Each mode opened, recorded its actual level and closed gracefully with exit 0. `docs/design/m6/probe-*.txt` are the raw reports. This records the platform'"'s reported level, not a visual endorsement of the compositor material.

## Visual QA and limits

- Repaired Card's clipped final text by revising vertical padding and reducing body to 16 DIP. The final main/bars/menu frames show the complete fixture including strike and last paragraph.
- Direct 144-DPI RTB rendering double-scaled nested card text and omitted menu/control children. Rejected those frames. Final renderer uses a fixed 960×800-DIP tree inside a Viewbox, explicitly scales the vector tree to 1×/1.5× and rasterizes via RTB at 96 DPI. This is new vector rasterization, not bitmap upsampling. Both scales now show the complete menu and consistent layout.
- Caret is real, shown after a render invalidation flush, at line 13 / column 21 in the indented task text. Empty states use a real empty document with a hint overlay; status reports line 1 / column 1 and zero words in Pro.
- Native Windows title bar/DWM shadow/corners and compositor backdrops cannot be captured by the client-tree RTB. Internal Card shadow/radii are actual opaque Avalonia Borders. No simulated desktop/backdrop is painted.
- Natural editor leading and flush-left code-panel text remain. Custom chevrons replace the harsh stock boxes without changing the installed folding manager. Offset-only scrolling/redraw, folding interaction and pointer target feel need hands-on validation before production integration.
- Main shows subdued bar opacity; bars shows full opacity and a More hover treatment. Hover-reveal and motion are proposals, intentionally not implemented in this design-selection task.
- Carousel frames are deterministic intermediate translations of two real editors; resting Card neighbour peeks are edge surfaces. They do not measure live animation quality. Card's dot range beyond eight notes still needs a production policy.
- The design host is a fixture/review mode, not a replacement resident shell: it never opens real notes or registers hotkeys/tray. More/pin/minimize/hide are real controls; New/Delete/navigation/menu-command layouts, rail search, and Settings are design affordances awaiting selected-direction integration. The in-tree menu is deliberate so RTB includes it; native popup behavior is not being claimed.

## Needs the user's eyes

1. Choose Quiet, Card or Pro by reviewing main **and** bars/menu/empty at both scales. Judge hierarchy, body weight, marker contrast and whether controls feel deliberate.
2. Quiet: subdued idle controls and writing inset. Card: available writing area, neighbour peeks and floating pager. Pro: density, rail usefulness and status/command-hint noise.
3. Open each live backdrop probe over light/dark content; inspect focus/deactivation, moving/resizing, text edges and monitor DPI changes. Mica/Acrylic were reported as granted; Blur was not.
4. After selection/integration: physical wheel/drag, checkbox/fold hit targets, focus-revealed bars, physical hotkey-to-paint and motion/reduced-motion behavior. Current performance evidence is bounded to scripted production-resident checks, not future animation or the new layouts integrated with persistence.

No git commands, network calls, STATUS.md/HANDOFF edits, or unrelated source changes. Manager owns git and selection follow-through. Per-direction checkpoints are in "'`.coord/status-T011.md`.
